      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 592,
        "height": 448,
        "content": "## VIX Data Preparation\n\nThis section prepares the market data for reliable comparison and classification. The VIX response is converted into a consistent structure, the previously stored regime is retrieved from Google Sheets, and the current VIX value is classified into LOW, NORMAL, ELEVATED, or CRISIS according to the configured thresholds."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e1ce4d36-4128-4a33-ad0f-8942e188f820",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2720,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 688,
        "height": 448,
        "content": "## AI Risk Context Generation\nThis section generates general educational risk-management context only after a genuine VIX regime transition is detected. OpenAI receives the already-classified regime and produces structured guidance about volatility and general position-sizing considerations. The response is normalized before the new VIX state is prepared for storage."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c8960e7e-82f6-402d-9a52-1f113224fe56",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -128,
        -112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 704,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "# VIX Regime Shift Detector\n\n## How it works\nThe workflow runs daily and retrieves the latest India VIX value, validates and normalizes the data, then classifies volatility as LOW, NORMAL, ELEVATED, or CRISIS. It compares the current regime with the previous state stored in Google Sheets. Only genuine regime transitions continue to OpenAI for general educational risk context. The updated state and transition history are stored in Google Sheets, and the completed alert is sent to Slack.\n## Setup Steps\n1. Create the VIX Regime Monitor Google Sheet with CurrentState and RegimeHistory sheets.\n2. Configure the existing Google Sheets, OpenAI, and Slack credentials in the corresponding n8n nodes.\n3. Keep the dummy VIX API for initial testing and use values such as 18.5, 24.7, and 32.4 to test different regime transitions.\n4. Confirm that NORMAL -> ELEVATED generates an AI response, updates Google Sheets, logs the transition, and sends one Slack alert.\n5. Confirm that ELEVATED -> ELEVATED does not generate an unnecessary Slack notification.\n6. After successful testing, replace Fetch India VIX Market Data with the real India VIX API while keeping its output compatible with the existing normalization node.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
